  - Vegan
  - Vegetarian
  - Dairy-Free
keywords: "cannabis weed canna coconut oil cannaoil recipe"
cuisine: "American"
prep_time:
  days:
  hours:
  minutes: 30
cook_time:
  days:
  hours: 4
  minutes:
total_time:
  days:
  hours: 4
  minutes: 30
yield:
  integer: 1
  text: 1 cup
equipment:
  - Crockpot
  - Tea towel
  - Mason jar(s) with lid(s)
  - Cheesecloth
ingredients:
  - "1 oz [decarboxylated cannabis](/edibles/decarb-activate-cannabis-edibles)"
  - 1.25 cups coconut oil, melted
directions:
  - Lay a clean [[affiliate:tea-towel]] in the bottom of your [[affiliate:crockpot]] to buffer the glass jar against the bottom of the crock. Add enough water to the crockpot to come at least 3/4 of the way to the top of your jar(s).
  - Stick a digital thermometer in your water bath and turn the crockpot on high. Allow the water bath to come up to 185°F and then turn to low.
  - While the crockpot is heating up, decarb your cannabis if you haven't already. Add the oil and decarboxylated cannabis to a clean mason jar and screw on the lid finger tight.
  - Place your sealed jar in the crock and cook on low for four hours, maintaining a temperature of 185°F.
  - After four hours strain your oil and weed through a fine-mesh strainer/cheesecloth into a clean container or jar. See our [straining notes](#straining-cannabis-infused-coconut-oil).
  - Allow the oil to cool.
  - Enjoy your oil, use it in [recipes](/edibles/), or see notes for [storage information](#storing-cannabis-infused-oil).
notes:
  - "For dosing help, try our [edibles dosage calculator](/edibles-calculator)."
  - This method is for the crock pot. See above for information on how to make [canna oil on a stove](#how-to-make-cannabis-infused-coconut-oil-on-a-stovetop) or in an [Ardent device](#how-to-make-cannabis-infused-coconut-oil-in-an-infusion-device).
